# jarvis-trader dashboard — conventions for Cursor

This is the Next.js 15 / React 19 dashboard for the JARVIS trading engine. It is a
**display + control surface only** — it never makes trading-safety decisions. All
safety/risk logic lives in the Python engine (`engine/risk/`), behind the API.

## Dev loop (read this first)
- **Package manager: `pnpm` only.** System `npm` is broken on this machine.
- **Hot-reload dev server:** `pnpm dev:cursor` runs on **port 3011**. Edit a file and
  preview at `http://127.0.0.1:3011` — instant. Do NOT use `pnpm dev` (port 3010) — that
  collides with the pm2 production dashboard.
- The pm2 **production** dashboard on **3010** runs `next start` (a static build). It does
  **not** hot-reload. Changes only appear there after `pnpm build` + `pm2 restart jarvis-dashboard`.
- **Before declaring done:** `pnpm typecheck` (runs `tsc --noEmit`) must pass. For a full
  check, `pnpm build` must succeed (it produces ~40 routes, 0 TS errors).

## Engine API access — non-negotiable
- **All engine calls go through `fetchEngine` / `postEngine` from `@/lib/api`.**
  Never use a bare `await fetch(...)`. Never hardcode `http://localhost:8010`,
  `127.0.0.1:8010`, or `:3010` in a component — the proxy + API key live in `lib/api.ts`
  and `next.config.ts` rewrites (`/api/engine` -> engine).
- Define response interfaces in `lib/api.ts` and import them. Do not redefine types locally.
- **No `any`.** TypeScript strict mode is on.

## Data fetching
- Use `useSWR` for polling/cached data (pass a `fetcher` that calls `fetchEngine`).
- Use `useState` + `useEffect` only for one-off fetches.

## Components & rendering
- **App Router:** default to Server Components. Add `"use client"` only when you need
  interactivity or browser APIs, and push the boundary as far down the tree as possible.
- Navigation lives in `components/Sidebar.tsx` (`NAV_GROUPS`). Add new pages there.
- New routes go under `app/<route>/page.tsx`.

## Styling
- **Tailwind only.** No inline styles, no CSS modules, no component libs beyond the
  existing `components/ui/*` (shadcn-style) and Radix primitives already in use.
- Use semantic tokens: `bg-background`, `bg-card`, `border-border`, `text-foreground`,
  `text-muted-foreground`, `text-accent`, and the trading colors `text-bull` / `text-bear`
  / `text-warn` / `text-info`.
- **Badges: use `<Badge variant=...>` from `@/components/ui/badge` with the strict set
  only:** `bull | bear | warn | info | neutral` (plus `live | static` for data-provenance
  honesty). Do not invent ad-hoc badge colors.

## General
- No emojis in code or comments.
- Conventional commits: `feat:`, `fix:`, `refactor:`, `docs:`, `chore:`. One change per commit.
- Never commit secrets. `dashboard/.env.local` holds the engine API key and is gitignored.
